{"id":"ddb3273a-31d0-4a7f-a69f-88021d84cc9f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"06da9ee11c0a1cf9","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/editor-state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"2b8352f9cafbe2c519366f0c6092f290283474b3","start":2277,"end":2410},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","pathOf","=","(","uri",":","vscodeApi",".","Uri",")",":","string","=>","(","uri",".","scheme","===","\"","file","\"","?","vscode",".","workspace",".","asRelativePath","(","uri",",","false",")",":","uri",".","toString","(",")",")"]},"context":{"before":"f114ddeee0a02ff7","after":"1d9b1951db35ac54"}},"payload":{"text":"A file's path in the workspace — relative, as the tools take it — or its URI when it isn't a file.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:19:03.906Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:19:03.906Z"}
{"id":"e73cd159-9d06-4776-b5f8-253dc0e42144","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/editor-state.ts","baseline":{"blob":"bef6a833924202b2b35daa954de0bed177ba5bdb","start":0,"end":46},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"2c1cb6475bc215a0"}},"payload":{"text":"What the editor shows, as data — for agents (the `editor_state`, `editor_problems` and `editor_notifications` tools, tools/),\nwhich would otherwise read it off the DOM or know VS Code's API and which frame it's in:\n\n- `editor.state`: the file in front of you — its cursor, selections and the lines in view, unsaved or not — and every\neditor tab open, by group;\n- `problems.list` { file?, limit? }: the Problems view's diagnostics, each with its source (TypeScript, eslint, notes,\na capability tripwire), severity, range and message;\n- `notifications.list`: the notifications showing — the toasts and the notification center's — which the extension API\ncan't list (the component reads the notification service's model);\n- `editor.trace` { component, seconds? }: VS Code's own log at trace, for a while, for one component — the messages\nnaming it (`text file model`, `extension host`) — forwarded into the editor's log stream (source `vscode-trace`),\nwhere logs_query and logs_wait read it. It answers at once; the window closes on its own. A person's way to the same:\n*Developer: Trace a VS Code Component…* (`editor.trace.show`), its messages in the Output channel \"VS Code Trace\" too.\n\nLines and columns are 1-based, as an agent reads code. Runs in the workbench realm (core), with its own extension API.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:19:12.596Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:19:12.596Z"}
